findings.description:
`tick.py` is typed against `SpatialQuery` but probes for an undeclared method with `hasattr`. That is a hidden interface, at odds with the architecture's "Clean boundaries" goal and the project rule to program to contracts.

It is also unnecessary. `AdaptiveSpatial.query_radius_batch` already returns the raw pre-cap `counts`. The wrapper can compute the signal there (subtracting the self-hit) and apply the switch on the next `build()`. That removes:
- the `tick.py` change and the `hasattr` guard;
- the guard test and the "Special Considerations" paragraph;
- the rejected-alternative discussion at line 164.

It also makes "the dispatcher is invisible upstream" (line 53) literally true. The near-duplicate "Data Flow" section (240-254) restates "Tick Integration" and can be cut too.
